sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch05-20> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "The flask-shaped (unduloid) shell of Lagena is formed while the organism hangs vertically, in a position of symmetry about its vertical axis, like a hanging drop; flattened or winged forms are those formed when this symmetry of position was absent and the shell lay horizontally.";
    dc:type "prediction";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The unduloid Lagena shell is formed while hanging vertically in the sea";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "D’Arcy Wentworth Thompson, On Growth and Form (1st ed., Cambridge: Cambridge University Press, 1917), Chapter V, “The Forms of Cells”; topic “Foraminiferal shells and position of symmetry”. Scope: monothalamous calcareous foraminifera (Lagena) and, by extension, flask-shaped pteropod shells"
}
